                                "sense_id": "bbdceed3-ce3a-3aff-b6b1-8ff7104d6b50",
                                "text": "Why do critics—some of them—make such short, smart work,—such cheerful, confident despatch, nowadays, of a story with religion in it, as if it were an abnormity,—a thing with sentence of death in itself, like a calf born with two heads,—that needs not their trouble, save to name it as it is?"
